# --- virtual environments (5.4 GB) ---------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
**/.venv/

# --- python caches --------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- CORPUS DATA: excluded for PRIVACY first, size second -----------------
#
# These are bulk scraped Indic web documents. The pipeline's stage 6 exists to
# strip PII from them (names, Aadhaar/PAN/phone patterns) - so the raw draws and
# the stage 1-5 intermediates are, by definition, text that has NOT yet been
# scrubbed. Publishing them would republish personal data harvested from the
# open web, which is the exact harm the DPDP-Act analysis in 3_40b_model and the
# stage-6 filter are written to prevent.
#
# The source datasets are public and CC-BY-4.0, so anyone can redraw them: every
# sample is reproducible from stage0_sample.py at a fixed offset and revision.
# Nothing here is lost - only the obligation to rehost it.
#
# They are also 1.9 GB and several exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
**/raw_sample/*.jsonl
**/work_*/
*.bin

# Frozen hand-label pool - same reasoning, 84 MB of raw web text.
**/telugu_quality_label_pool.jsonl

# --- benchmark test items -------------------------------------------------
# Fetched copies of public eval test splits (GSM8K, MMLU, HumanEval, MBPP,
# Belebele, ARC). Already public, but rehosting test items in a training-data
# repo is contamination-adjacent housekeeping we would rather not do.
# `python decon/measure.py --fetch` regenerates them in about a minute.
decon/benchmarks/*.jsonl
**/decon/benchmarks/*.jsonl

# --- saved browser pages --------------------------------------------------
# "Save Page As" captures of the course platform: 91 files, 8.6 MB, 57 of them
# minified third-party JS bundles. Not our work, not a deliverable, and 29% of
# the repo's file count. Kept locally, not published.
**/Axiom*Learning OS.html
**/Axiom*Learning OS_files/

# --- build outputs ---------------------------------------------------------
# site.html IS committed (it is the readable deliverable). The fragment is the
# same content minus its doctype/head/body, kept only for Artifact publishing,
# and build_site.py regenerates it - no reason to store it twice.
site.fragment.html

# --- local scratch --------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
